\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Hazard-identification accuracy on the 19-scene SafeLIBERO benchmark as a function of how much authority the VLM is given. Whole-scene VLM identification tops out at 84\% even at API strength (local models: 18--64\%); letting a VLM \emph  {compose} the rule at runtime is worse than the fixed rule; grounding Eq.\nobreakspace  {}\textup  {\hbox {\mathsurround \z@ \normalfont  (\ignorespaces \ref  {eq:fol}\unskip \@@italiccorr )}}'s predicates with cached VLM priors reaches 84\% top-1 and \textbf  {100\% top-2 guard-set recall} --- the deployed configuration --- matching the hand-coded predicate table it replaces.}}{6}{figure.3}}
\newlabel{fig:vlmacc}{{3}{6}{Hazard-identification accuracy on the 19-scene SafeLIBERO benchmark as a function of how much authority the VLM is given. Whole-scene VLM identification tops out at 84\% even at API strength (local models: 18--64\%); letting a VLM \emph {compose} the rule at runtime is worse than the fixed rule; grounding Eq.~\eqref {eq:fol}'s predicates with cached VLM priors reaches 84\% top-1 and \textbf {100\% top-2 guard-set recall} --- the deployed configuration --- matching the hand-coded predicate table it replaces}{figure.3}{}}
